<BaseLayout title="About — Oliverse" description="About Oliver, an SMIX student learning AI, IT systems and automation in Barcelona." lang="en"><section class="page-hero shell"><p class="eyebrow">About me</p><h1>Curious by default.<br /><em>Practical by choice.</em></h1><p>I’m Oliver, an SMIX student in Barcelona. I want to understand how technology works and turn that curiosity into projects that show care, clarity and a drive to keep learning.</p></section><section class="about-grid shell"><div class="about-copy"><h2>Learning by doing.</h2><p>My interest in artificial intelligence grew by watching technology creators such as Nate Gentile explain not only what AI could do, but how it could interact with real systems and tools. When I discovered OpenClaw, I thought: “I want to build my own.”</p><p>I repurposed a computer, installed Ubuntu Server and started experimenting. That became Coco—my personal assistant and the project through which I am learning about automation, systems, privacy and the real limits of AI.</p><p>I also enjoy hardware, technical support, networks and cybersecurity. My goal is to build strong foundations, make things with care and leave visitors with a sense of curiosity, positive energy and attention to detail.</p></div><div class="focus-card"><p class="eyebrow">Current focus</p><ul><li><span>01</span>Applied artificial intelligence</li><li><span>02</span>Automation &amp; assistants</li><li><span>03</span>IT support, systems &amp; networks</li><li><span>04</span>Clear technical documentation</li></ul></div></section></BaseLayout>
